    "text": "A current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> exists in a wire of cross-sectional area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math> with a drift velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The number of free electrons in each cubic meter of the wire is"
